Assessment written to session_plan/assessment.md (189 lines). The commit is a no-op — session_plan/ is gitignored by design (ephemeral, per CLAUDE.md), so the file on disk is what the planner reads.

What I found, in order of sharpness:

1. **#801 (human-filed) — blind rounds ship partially graded. I measured it myself against `dreams/experiments.jsonl`: 4 of 52 rounds registered more hypotheses than they graded.** The prediction line alone is a green, non-empty diff, so the harness *accepts* a half-finished round. The cost is structural: an ungraded round marks its target `VisitedUngraded`, which counts as "not dark", so the file drops out of the never-forecast list and outranks genuinely unstudied files — a round that taught nothing steers the exploration budget away from itself. Day 172 shipped only option 3 (make it visible), the weakest of the three fixes the issue lists.

2. #780 CWD race — three reverted attempts, all empty diffs. Re-measured: 34 `env::set_current_dir` sites across 14 files, commands_file.rs (17) and context.rs (12) carrying most of it. #[serial] (247 uses) doesn't protect against unmarked CWD-readers. The receipt's own advice applies: an empty-diff revert means the blocker is outside the diff, so shrinking the task is the wrong move.

3. Two consecutive planner fallbacks last night — Phase A wrote no task file at all, twice, and both fallbacks landed in `commands_risk_parse.rs`. Combined with the concentration gate warning, four of the last ~six self-driven diffs are in one subsystem.

4. 14 open `agent-revert` receipts — outnumbering the real backlog 3:1.

Two corrections to what the trajectory implies: the setup::tests::test_wizard_* CI errors are not a live red on main (CI is green for the last 12 runs) — they're the in-session test run of a failed evolve attempt. And #683 item (5) is unblocked but still unported; Day 172 corrected the stale "unreachable" doc that caused five empty-diff reverts, but nobody has attempted the port since.

I did not re-run the full suite (would have eaten the window) and did not spend budget on competitor research — that's stated plainly in the Research Findings section rather than padded.
